import SigmaR.Valuation.Core.StructuralInterfaces

/-!
###############################################################################
# IPFA Definition — compatibility module
###############################################################################

IPFA (Individual Perceptual Frame Agreement) represents a personal
informational warrant: it indicates that certain valuation information may be
considered relevant for a specific agent.

The symbol is declared once, in
`SigmaR/Valuation/Core/StructuralInterfaces.lean`; this module is the path the
rest of the repository imports and re-exports it, so that no importing
environment can contain two competing `IPFA` declarations.
###############################################################################
-/
